The prose samples in this directory are NOT covered by the repository's MIT
licence. They are EFF Deeplinks posts, redistributed under:

    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY 4.0)
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The grant, quoted from https://www.eff.org/copyright ("Creative Commons"):

    "Any and all original material on the EFF website may be freely
     distributed at will under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
     International License (CC-BY), unless otherwise noted. All material
     that is not original to EFF may require permission from the copyright
     holder to redistribute."

Deeplinks posts are original EFF material. Redistribution must carry the
attribution: Electronic Frontier Foundation, eff.org, plus the named author
and permalink recorded per file in ATTRIBUTION.json and in each file's
frontmatter. Nothing here has been modified beyond markup removal.

The two caveats in EFF's grant are handled, not waved past.
`fetch-professional.mjs` refuses any post whose body carries a competing
copyright or licence line, because "unless otherwise noted" means such a note
overrides the site-wide grant; and no post is vendored that consists mainly of
reprinted third-party text, because "not original to EFF" is not EFF's to
license.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIS DIRECTORY IS MULTI-AUTHOR. IT IS NOT A VOICE CORPUS.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Deeplinks is a staff blog: roughly 27 named authors across 50 posts, and no
author has enough samples here to characterise an individual's cadence. What
you get by averaging them is a house style.

    human-essays/         SINGLE identifiable authors, >=15 samples each.
                          This is what voice calibration and the voice
                          critic's cross-author test may use.

    human-professional/   THIS directory. Many authors, one register.
                          Register coverage only. Never a voice corpus.

    human/                Wikipedia, many editors per article. Same kind of
                          thing as this directory, different register.

The distinction is load-bearing. Anything that reasons about voice assumes
"these samples were written by the same person"; that assumption is false
here, and a tool that took it on faith would report a confident measurement of
a person who does not exist.

One overlap to know about: Cory Doctorow writes for Deeplinks and also has his
own single-author tranche in `human-essays/pluralistic/`. Cross-author work
must draw from one bucket, not both, or it will score an author against
himself and call the result a match.

Nothing may be added to this directory except text that is public domain or
under a licence at least as permissive - CC0, CC-BY, or CC-BY-SA - with the
grant quotable and the provenance recorded per file. Not contemporary
journalism outside such a licence, not private writing, however good a sample
it would make.
